[[File:Kasugasui.jpeg|thumb|250px|right|Kasuga Spring (春日水)]] '''Kasuga Shrine''' (春日神社) is a {{ill|Shinto shrine|ja|神社|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shinto shrine|qq=}} located in {{ill|Myozan, Tokushima City|ja|眉山町|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Myozan, Tokushima City|qq=}}, {{ill|Tokushima Prefecture|ja|徳島県|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tokushima Prefecture|qq=}}, Japan. It is situated on the eastern foothills of {{ill|Mount Bizan|ja|眉山|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mount Bizan|qq=}}.
== Deities == The shrine enshrines the following four {{ill|Kami|ja|柱|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kami|qq=}} (deities), identical to those of {{ill|Kasuga Taisha|ja|春日大社|1=Kasuga-taisha|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga Taisha|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga-taisha|qq=}} in {{ill|Nara Prefecture|ja|奈良県|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Nara Prefecture|qq=}}: * {{ill|Takemikazuchi|ja|武甕槌命|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takemikazuchi|qq=}} * {{ill|Izanagi-no-Mikoto|ja|斎主命|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Izanagi-no-Mikoto|qq=}} * {{ill|Amenokoyane no Mikoto|ja|天児屋根命|1=Ame-no-Koyane|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Amenokoyane no Mikoto|13=User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Koyane|qq=}} * {{ill|Hime no Kami|ja|比売神|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hime no Kami|qq=}}
== History == The shrine traces its origins to a {{ill|Kasuga Shrine|ja|春日祠|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga Shrine|qq=}} enshrined at the Kasuga territory in {{ill|Tomi-da|ja|富田庄|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tomi-da|qq=}} (modern {{ill|Irida|ja|入田町|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Irida|qq=}}, Tokushima City), a former estate of Kasuga Shrine in {{ill|Yamato Province|ja|大和国|qq=Yamato Province|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Yamato Province|qq=}}. It is said to have been relocated to its current site at Otakiyama during the transfer of power to the {{ill|Hachisuka clan|ja|蜂須賀氏|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hachisuka clan|qq=}} in 1586, coinciding with the construction of {{ill|Tokushima Castle|ja|徳島城|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tokushima Castle|qq=}}. Another account suggests the shrine was moved from {{ill|Tamiya Village|ja|田宮村|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tamiya Village|qq=}} along with Shofuku-ji Temple, which later became the shrine’s {{ill|Bettōji|ja|別当寺|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bettōji|qq=}} before its abolition in the early {{ill|Meiji period|ja|明治|lt=Meiji period|1=Meiji era|2=ja|3=明治|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Meiji period|qq=}}.<ref>According to the ''Awa-shi'' (阿波志), compiled in 1815.</ref>
During the {{ill|Keicho era|ja|慶長|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Keicho era|qq=}} (late 16th to early 17th century), the shrine was referred to as "Kasuga Daimyōjin" and received significant patronage from the Hachisuka clan, including an annual offering of 10 koku of rice. In 1873, it was officially renamed Kasuga Shrine and designated as a {{ill|Ken-sha|ja|県社|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ken-sha|qq=}}. The shrine also features "Kasuga Spring" (春日水), one of the notable {{ill|Mount Bizan springs|ja|眉山湧水群|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Mount Bizan springs|qq=}}.
== Sub-Shrines == The shrine complex includes the following sub-shrines: * '''Toyotama-hime Shrine''' (deity: {{ill|Toyotama-hime|ja|豊玉比賣|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Toyotama-hime|qq=}}) ** Enshrines the deity formerly worshipped at Ryuo Shrine within Tokushima Castle. * '''Wakamiya Shrine''' (deity: {{ill|Ame-no-Kumunushi|ja|天忍雲根命|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Kumunushi|qq=}}) * '''Akiba Shrine''' (deity: {{ill|Amaterasu|ja|天照大御神|1=Amaterasu|lt=Amaterasu Ōmikami|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Amaterasu|13=User:Immanuelle/Amaterasu|qq=}}, {{ill|Onamuchi|ja|大巳貴命|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Onamuchi|qq=}}, {{ill|Haniyasubime|ja|埴安姫神|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Haniyasubime|qq=}}, {{ill|Ukemochi|ja|保食神|1=Ukemochi|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ukemochi|13=User:Immanuelle/Ukemochi|qq=}}, {{ill|Sukunabikona|ja|少彦名命|1=Sukunabikona|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Sukunabikona|13=User:Immanuelle/Sukunabikona|qq=}})
== Transportation == * '''By car''': 5 minutes from {{ill|Tokushima Station|ja|徳島駅|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tokushima Station|qq=}}, {{ill|Shikoku Railway Company|ja|四国旅客鉄道|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shikoku Railway Company|qq=}} (JR Shikoku).
