==Merged second translation== {{otheruses|A Shinto shrine in Bizan Town, Tokushima City|A Shinto shrine in Shimosuketo Town, Tokushima City|{{ill|Kasuga Shrine (Tokushima City, Shimosuketo)|ja|春日神社 (徳島市下助任町)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga Shrine (Tokushima City, Shimosuketo)|qq=}}}} {{Infobox religious building| religious_affiliation = [[Shinto]] |name = Kasuga Shrine |image = [[File:Kasuga Jinjya.jpeg|250px]] |location = [[Tokushima Prefecture|Tokushima]], [[Tokushima City|Tokushima City]], {{ill|Bizan Town|ja|眉山町|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bizan Town|qq=}} Ōtakiyama 1 |位置 = {{ウィキ座標2段度分秒|34|04|19.9|N|134|32|33.4|E|scale:25000|display=inline,title}} |deity = [[Takemikazuchi-no-Mikoto]], [[Amenokoyane-no-Mikoto]], [[Amenooshihi-no-Mikoto]], [[Hime-no-Kami]] |type = Former Prefectural Shrine |創建 = Tenshō 14 (1586) |別名 = |札所等 = Tokushima City Central Five Shrines |本殿 = [[Kasuga-zukuri]] |festival = [[:en:April 17|April 17]], [[:en:October 17|October 17]] |神事 = }}
'''Kasuga Shrine''' (春日神社) is a Shinto shrine located in {{ill|Bizan Town|ja|眉山町|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bizan Town|qq=}}, [[Tokushima (city)|Tokushima City]], [[Tokushima Prefecture|Tokushima Prefecture]], Japan. It is situated at the eastern foot of Mount Ōtakiyama within Bizan.
== Enshrined Deities == The shrine venerates the {{ill|Kasuga-no-Kami|fr|Kasuga_no_Kami|ja|春日神|1=Kasuga-no-Kami|2=ja|3=春日神|4=fr|5=Kasuga no Kami|6=zh|7=春日權現|8=wuu|9=春日權現|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga-no-Kami|13=User:Immanuelle/Kasuga-no-Kami|qq=}} just like that of [[Kasuga-taisha]] {| class="wikitable" !Shrine facility ![[Shinto]] part ![[:en:Buddhism|Buddhism]] part |- |first hall<ref name="www.kasugataisha.or.jp">{{Cite web|title=Main Sanctuary|url=http://www.kasugataisha.or.jp/guidance/map3/k_map01.html|url-status=dead|archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20190624041142/http://www.kasugataisha.or.jp/guidance/map3/k_map01.html|archive-date=2019-06-24|access-date=2019-03-28|website=www.kasugataisha.or.jp}}</ref> |{{ill|Takemikazuchi|en|4=fr|lt=Takemikazuchi-o|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Takemikazuchi|qq=}} |{{ill|Amoghapasha|ja|不空羂索観音|fr|Amoghapasha Lokeshvara|id|Arca Amoghapasa|jv|Arca Amoghapasa|zh|不空羂索觀音|simple|User:Immanuelle/Amoghapasha|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Amoghapasha|qq=}}<ref>https://kuscholarworks.ku.edu/bitstream/1808/17426/1/Fowler.pdf</ref> |- |second hall<ref name="www.kasugataisha.or.jp" /> |{{ill|Futsunushi|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Futsunushi|qq=}} |{{ill|Bhaisajyaguru|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bhaisajyaguru|qq=}} |- |third hall<ref name="www.kasugataisha.or.jp" /> |{{ill|Ame-no-Koyane|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ame no Koyane|qq=}} |{{ill|Kṣitigarbha|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kṣitigarbha|qq=}} |- |fourth hall<ref name="www.kasugataisha.or.jp" /> |{{ill|Himegami|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Himegami|qq=}} |{{ill|Ekādaśamukha|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ekādaśamukha|qq=}} |- |Wakamiya Shrine<ref name="https">https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/common/001559851.pdf</ref><ref name="Japan Tourism Agency,Japan Tourism Agency">{{Cite web|title=Wakamiya Shrine {{!}} Search Details|url=https://www.mlit.go.jp/tagengo-db/en/H30-00882.html|access-date=2024-03-20|website=Japan Tourism Agency,Japan Tourism Agency|language=en}}</ref> |{{ill|Ame-no-Oshikumone|ja|天押雲根命|en|draft:Ame-no-Oshikumone|simple|User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|fr|Utilisateur:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|qq=}} |[[:en:Manjushri|Manjushri]] or {{ill|Avalokiteśvara|en|4=fr|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Avalokiteśvara|qq=}}.<ref name="Giolai-2020">{{Cite journal|last=Giolai|first=Andrea|date=2020-09-22|title=Encounters with the Past: Fractals and Atmospheres at Kasuga Wakamiya Onmatsuri|url=https://brill.com/view/journals/jrj/9/1-3/article-p213_8.xml|journal=Journal of Religion in Japan|volume=9|issue=1-3|pages=213–247|doi=10.1163/22118349-00901002|issn=2211-8349}}</ref> |}
== History == The shrine traces its origins to a Kasuga Shrine originally enshrined in {{ill|Tomida Manor|ja|富田庄|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tomida Manor|qq=|ja_comment=jawiki [[Category:Kasuga Redirects]]s to 富田荘}} of [[:en:Yamato Province|Yamato Province]] (present-day {{ill|Iritamura|ja|入田村|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Iritamura|qq=}} in [[Tokushima City|Tokushima City]]). During the invasion of [[Awa Province]] by [[:en:Hachisuka Iemasa|Hachisuka Iemasa]], the shrine was relocated to its current location at Ōtakiyama 1 in {{ill|Bizan Town|ja|眉山町|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bizan Town|qq=}}. This history is documented in the *Awa-shi* from 1815 (Bunka 12). Another theory suggests that in 1586 (Tenshō 14), during the construction of [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokushima_Castle Tokushima Castle], the shrine was moved from {{ill|Tamiyamura|ja|田宮村|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Tamiyamura|qq=}} to serve as the castle's tutelary shrine.
Under the governance of the [[:en:Hachisuka clan|Hachisuka clan]], the shrine, known as "Kasuga Daimyōjin," gained significant reverence, receiving annual offerings of 10 koku of rice. In 1873 (Meiji 6), the shrine's name was officially changed to Kasuga Shrine, and it was designated a Prefectural Shrine. The site includes the spring known as *Kasuga Water*, part of the {{ill|Bizan Springs|ja|眉山湧水群|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Bizan Springs|qq=}}.
== Subsidiary Shrines == * '''Toyotama-Hime Shrine''' (deity: [[Toyotama-hime|Toyotama-Hime-no-Mikoto]], designated as an ancient shrine) ''' The shrine was originally located within [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokushima_Castle Tokushima Castle] as Ryūō Shrine, later merged into Kunikazu Shrine before being relocated here. * '''Wakamiya Shrine''' (deity: {{ill|Ame-no-Oshikumone|ja|天押雲根命|en|draft:Ame-no-Oshikumone|simple|User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|fr|Utilisateur:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Ame-no-Oshikumone|qq=}}) * '''Akiba Shrine''' (deity: [[Amaterasu]], [[Ōkuninushi|Ōkuninushi-no-Mikoto]], [[Haniyasu-hiko and Haniyasu-hime|Haniyasu-hime-no-Mikoto]], [[:en:Ukemochi|Ukemochi-no-Kami]], [[Sukunabikona|Sukunahikona-no-Kami]])
== Transportation == * Approximately 5 minutes by car from [[JR Tokushima Station]].
== Related Articles == * Tokushima City Central Five Shrines: ''' {{ill|Suwa Shrine (Tokushima City)|ja|諏訪神社 (徳島市)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Suwa Shrine (Tokushima City)|qq=}} - Located in Minamisako, Tokushima City ''' {{ill|Shisho Shrine (Tokushima)|ja|四所神社 (徳島市)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Shisho Shrine (Tokushima City)|qq=}} - Located in Fukushima, Tokushima City ''' {{ill|Hachiman Shrine (Tokushima City)|ja|八幡神社 (徳島市)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Hachiman Shrine (Tokushima City)|qq=}} - Located in Iga Town, Tokushima City ''' {{ill|Konpira Shrine (Tokushima)|ja|金刀比羅神社 (徳島市)|qq=draft|qq=draft|qq=draft|12=simple|13=User:Immanuelle/Kotohira Shrine (Tokushima City)|qq=}} - Located in Semimachi, Tokushima City
